340-When Codex is maintaining reflection against a governing guide, use these anchor routes:
341-
342:- Prompt Chaining / Planning -> base prompts; keep staged dependency, checkpoint, and fallback visibility explicit instead of collapsing into one-shot execution language
343-- Routing / Prioritization / Exploration -> `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay`; prefer `Resource budget and route-choice memo` or `Prioritization queue / next-action memo`
344-- Parallelization / Multi-Agent / A2A -> `PROMPT_multi_agent_overlay` + `orchestration-control`; prefer `Delegation admission memo`, `A2A task-handoff memo`, and `Join-quality review memo`
345-- Tool Use / MCP -> `PROMPT_tool_protocol_overlay`; prefer `Tool capability contract / precondition memo` or `MCP capability handoff memo`
346-- Memory / Learning / Adaptation -> `PROMPT_memory_adaptation_overlay`; prefer `Memory scope / checkpoint profile memo`, `Learning-signal review memo`, and `Adaptation decision memo`
347-- Goal / Monitoring / Recovery / HITL -> base prompts; prefer `Goal-monitoring status memo`, `Recovery / escalation checkpoint memo`, and `HITL approval packet`
348-- Retrieval / RAG -> `PROMPT_retrieval_grounding_overlay` + `grounded-research`; prefer `Evidence target / retrieval-mode memo` or `Source consultation ledger`
349-- Resource-Aware Optimization -> base prompts plus `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay`; prefer `Resource budget and route-choice memo`
350-- Reasoning Techniques / Reflection -> `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay`; prefer `Critique quality review memo` when critique utility or no-gain loops are under review
351:- Appendix A / advanced prompting execution families -> `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay` for decomposition, step-back, self-consistency, ReAct-like loops, tree-style search, and bounded reflection; keep prompt chaining in base prompts and treat example-catalog references as structure-only
352-- Appendix B / GUI, browser, device, or computer-use interaction -> `PROMPT_tool_protocol_overlay` plus base environment classes; add `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay` when visual/action-observation loops, intermediate state checks, or perception-driven replans materially matter
353-- Appendix C / framework overview, Appendix D / product build walkthrough, and Appendix F / reasoning-engine internals -> informational comparison/background only; do not treat named frameworks, product tutorials, or descriptive internals as first-pass normative owners of runtime policy
354-- Appendix E / CLI agents -> base prompts plus `coding-core` and `PROMPT_tool_protocol_overlay`; keep `cli_or_local_filesystem` and `ide_or_coding_agent` risk classes, repo-scope discipline, and approval boundaries explicit
355-- Appendix G / coding agents -> `CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE`, `coding-core`, and `orchestration-control` when specialist collaboration is real; keep human-led orchestration, reviewer/test ownership, and bounded patch verification explicit
